484	/// the jj CLI's) refuses to start tracking a *new* file over 1 MiB — `SnapshotOptions`'
485	/// `max_new_file_size`, the CLI's own `snapshot.max-new-file-size` default — so a born-oversized
486	/// fixture would never be tracked and never reach the diff at all. jj's gate applies only to files
487	/// it isn't already tracking, so growing a tracked one is snapshotted without complaint.
